invariant: INV-11
file: srv_flight.c
catches: srv_flight_test
reason: the server binds each direction to the opposite handshake secret
  from the client, and this restores handshake.c:94-95's client
  assignment inside the server. Nothing else in the tree says which side
  takes which: ks_handshake writes the client secret before the server one
  and names no endpoint, so a swapped pair compiles, derives both secrets
  correctly and fails every real client at the first protected record.
  docs/server.md, "The direction swap, in three lines", names this mutant
  and says it would otherwise pass every check here.

--- old
    rec_dir_init(&t->rd, h->c_hs);
    rec_dir_init(&t->wr, h->s_hs);
--- new
    rec_dir_init(&t->rd, h->s_hs);
    rec_dir_init(&t->wr, h->c_hs);
